{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends", "label": "ADR 0014: Jira sends the brief, and the read-only rule bends by allow-list", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/adr/0014-jira-sends-the-brief-and-the-read-only-rule-bends.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends_jira_notify_send", "label": "Jira sends the brief via issue notify; nothing leaves", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0014-jira-sends-the-brief-and-the-read-only-rule-bends.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "POST /rest/api/3/issue/{key}/notify sends mail through Jira's own machinery, so item 3 crosses no boundary. Recipients are Jira identities never addresses (a config leak discloses interest, not contact details); restrict drops recipients who lack BROWSE on the anchor at send time; no attachments, so the two views ship as static HTML in the body rather than the self-contained file."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends_restrict_browse", "label": "restrict: BROWSE filters recipients against the anchor issue only", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0014-jira-sends-the-brief-and-the-read-only-rule-bends.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Permission filtering enforced by the platform rather than asserted by the app, but partial: it restricts against the one issue the notification hangs off, not every issue the brief counts."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends_scope_allow_list", "label": "The read-only rule becomes an allow-list with justifications", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0014-jira-sends-the-brief-and-the-read-only-rule-bends.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "startswith('read:') in tests/test_service.py could not admit send:notification:jira and storage:app. Neither is write access to customer data. The test now lists permitted scopes and every non-read entry must carry a written justification; adding a scope stays a deliberate edit with a reason. Writing config to a Jira project property was rejected because it needs a write scope into Jira."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends_project_admin_recipients", "label": "Project administrators decide who receives a board", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0014-jira-sends-the-brief-and-the-read-only-rule-bends.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A recipient list is a disclosure control, not a display preference. Checked against Jira's own /mypermissions ADMINISTER_PROJECTS answer. Site admins were rejected because putting one person between every team and their board is how a feature stays switched off."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends_outgoing_mail_site_setting", "label": "Outgoing mail is a site setting, not a scope", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0014-jira-sends-the-brief-and-the-read-only-rule-bends.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Proved 2026-08-26: 'Outgoing emails disabled' 403. sendBrief quotes Jira's errorMessages because a bare 403 is indistinguishable between three fixes; the precondition belongs in the Marketplace listing."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends_people_picker_allow_list", "label": "People picker searches by name, stores the id, projects to an allow-list of fields", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0014-jira-sends-the-brief-and-the-read-only-rule-bends.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nobody knows colleagues' account ids. The app never maps an email to an account (an identity claim it has no standing to make); a human picks from Jira's matches, searched as the reader. user/search returns emailAddress etc., so people.js builds each match from an allow-list of two fields \u2014 a deny-list is one Atlassian release from leaking. Stored ids resolve back to names with a third field, state, because live, deactivated and missing have different fixes."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends_compose_js_injected", "label": "forge/src/compose.js keeps the send provable without deploying", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0014-jira-sends-the-brief-and-the-read-only-rule-bends.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "index.js imports the Forge SDK and cannot load outside Atlassian's runtime; the code deciding what reaches an inbox has the model and the send injected so tests supply stubs."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends", "target": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends_jira_notify_send", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0014-jira-sends-the-brief-and-the-read-only-rule-bends.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends", "target": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends_restrict_browse", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0014-jira-sends-the-brief-and-the-read-only-rule-bends.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends", "target": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends_scope_allow_list", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0014-jira-sends-the-brief-and-the-read-only-rule-bends.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends", "target": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends_project_admin_recipients", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0014-jira-sends-the-brief-and-the-read-only-rule-bends.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends", "target": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends_outgoing_mail_site_setting", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0014-jira-sends-the-brief-and-the-read-only-rule-bends.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends", "target": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends_people_picker_allow_list", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0014-jira-sends-the-brief-and-the-read-only-rule-bends.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends", "target": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends_compose_js_injected", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0014-jira-sends-the-brief-and-the-read-only-rule-bends.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0014_jira_sends_the_brief_and_the_read_only_rule_bends", "targ